{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1564346-help-with-a-bloodline-and-discpline","id":1564346,"title":"Help with a bloodline and discpline","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-09-26T03:22:18-07:00","id":1564346,"title":"Help with a bloodline and discpline","content":"Hello, I have an idea for a bloodline and a bloodline specific discipline but I'm not confident with much of the numbers and don't know what to do with a lot of the discipline.<br /> A short summary of what I have so far:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Perdices (Perdix, singular)</span><br /> <br /> Vampires roughly based on the tale of Icarus. (In short, vampire starts flying at night, flies far enough to begin to see the edge sunlight, peeking over the horizon, is overwhelmed by beauty and pain and falls into the ocean, barely surviving getting back to land. Can't fly too high or low because both sun and sea will kill you. The descendants are filled with desperate longing for the sun, and can call a small measure of it's warmth but even that small measure hurts them.)<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan:</b> Ventrue (I like the idea of Ventrue for this but Gangrel's Protean and Daeva's Majesty seem like they may fit better)<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames:</b> Partridges, Slugs, or (Something day/sun related? My mind just keeps shouting &quot;Sun-huggers&quot; at me but I don't think that works)<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Caustic Curse)</b>: <br /> The dead bodies of the kindred recoil and dissolve in the presence of a few substances. Fire and sunlight are universal and individuals may have personal banes which harm them to a lesser degree. The Perdices suffer from the touch of an additional substance, salt, and have their banes quickened in the presence of a catalyst, water. Salt acts upon a Perdix much like fire does, increasing in damage to undead flesh depending on the quantity of salt present. It deals (Lethal or aggravated, I don't know which would be better) every turn he stays in contact with it, with the exception of eating foods or otherwise consuming salt, that damage only occurs once. Extremely minor quantities, like those that can be found in a mortal's blood or just being near an ocean, does nothing of note, being too minor to have an effect. When a Perdix's banes are accompanied by water, increase the effective size/intensity of fire and salt by 1 and reduce the vampires effective humanity by 2 for the purpose of calculating damage and dice pool restrictions for all other bans/banes. (If on fire and someone douses them with water, the fire will grow larger and more voracious, rather than getting put out.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 100px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 2px; padding: 1px\"><b>Quantity of Salt</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 2px; padding: 1px\"><b>Damage</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 2px; padding: 1px\">Tablespoon</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 2px; padding: 1px\">1</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 2px; padding: 1px\">Large Mound</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 2px; padding: 1px\">2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 2px; padding: 1px\">Buried</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 2px; padding: 1px\">3</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <b>Favored Attributes:</b> Intelligence or Resolve<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Auspex, <i>Heliskos </i>(Rough mangling of Greek that <i>should</i> mean something like &quot;little sun&quot;. I used Google and Wikipedia so I am very uncertain), Resilience and (Either Majesty or Protean would work best, I think, although Dominate could work? Protean would mostly be there for Patagia/Wings, Majesty would mostly be there to have people look to them for their ideas and (alongside Dominate) to sweep them up into their obsessions and ideals.) (Heliskos would be a rough transfer from something I vaguely remember when reading about Vt Masquerade disciplines. I remember one that had vampires throw fire that they were still vulnerable to. In order to satisfy the &quot;every discipline should spread the curse into the world&quot; thing, the fire spreads the curse into the ash of what it consumes. It would have a few devotions, some more abstract than others (eg. a devotion including either Majesty or Dominate that lets you set an object of desire for the target or something along those lines). First dot would just be summoning a small flame on your finger which begins to burn after a round, not too sure about progression from there)<br /> <br /> <b>In Covenants: </b>Most common in the Lancea et Sanctum and second most common in the Ordo Dracul (Mystery of the Ascendant). In the Lancea et Sanctum, they see the sun as a gift of God's/God/a symbol of God's love and wish to receive God's grace in any way they can. In the Ordo Dracul, they wish to stay in the sun indefinitely, generally seeking the path of the Mystery of the Ascendant. <br /> <br /> Where am I going wrong and how could I improve it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29166-autonymos","name":"Autonymos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-26T04:47:53-07:00","id":1564351,"title":"","content":"The Discipline you remember is probably the Path of Fire from Thaumaturgy. I'm unsure if it fits the overall image you're trying to paint.<br /> <br /> First thing you have to do is tighten concept. It seems pretty vague for now: the reference to Icarus is only vaguely related to the Bane and Discipline, that seem disconnected, and your considerations for clan and other Disciplines hint to further ideas not properly formalized.<br /> <br /> Why it is the way it is? What is it trying to be? What is important about it? What narrative role will it accomplish? Why each given detail is there?<br /> <br /> I can say that the double Bane of salt and water seems really weird. If you want them to avoid the sea, make them weak to the sea, not to its individual components. Maybe longing for the sea then weak to its touch. Salt looks particularly incongruous and needing too many arbitrary exceptions to work.<br /> <br /> Heliskos as just fire throwing seems thematically weak. You can model it on the Physical Disciplines to have a few distinct effects that scale with level, or make a more usual spread of powers and let throwing fire be just one, scaling with Vitae expenditure if anything.<br /> <br /> Do not just copy the Path of Fire. Look for other fire related effects in other lines and games for inspiration, or change the Discipline to really be about the sun.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-26T07:48:48-07:00","id":1564355,"title":"","content":"Building on monte's observations, I would add that if the goal is to replicate the vibe of Icarus in the myth, Daeva is probably your best fit as the clan whose archetype hews closest to the &quot;young passionate vampire that gets caught up in trouble due to a lapse in judgment&quot; that suits &quot;Got too excited to be free from imprisonment and was destroyed by the limitations of his means of escape.&quot; (The compelling nature of Majesty also fits if the goal is for them to draw people to them, and Vigor has provided a jump-booster specifically as a possible source of stories of flying vampires.)<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I see a reason for Auspex to be on their Discpline list, and presently there look to be three different core power concepts pulling in different directions. Are they supposed to be about flight, inspiring obsession, or producing fire? There are ways to make these things cohesive, but presently they're loose ideas vaguely connected to the Icarus myth \u2014 the bloodline can certainly do more than one thing, but as a bloodline instead of a clan or covenant it lacks the assumed breadth of membership to have its specific abilities not be rooted in the same source. Subtler/less literal powers get a bit more latitude of concept in addition to being less risk to the Masquerade, which may also be worth considering.<br /> <br /> Complementing the broader thematic questions about the Perdices, it is important to ask What They Do, which is itself informed by whether the bloodline was deliberately developed or spontaneously formed. Is this the product of some sort of blood alchemy or a chance encounter with a sirenic muse? Are they known as visionaries, explorers, liberators? Are they a cult, a political movement, a magical think tank?<br /> <br /> Pinning down specifics will help build momentum toward getting concrete ideas formed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-26T11:56:48-07:00","id":1564365,"title":"","content":"One important point is to not lock yourself into a clan because it has powers you want. The power list can be tweaked later.<br /> <br /> Instead, use a clan that fits story and themes, especially their Bane. Daeva is a no-brainer for the passion angle, while others may fit specific dramatic goals.<br /> <br /> Choosing powers and clan are downstream of refining concept, though, or you'll end up with something whose pieces seem to follow the same reference, but still don't form a cohesive whole.<br /> <br /> And just to be clear, there's zero problem with starting design from the &quot;I want to have this&quot; state. Having the specific list of powers may be the actual point. But you have to make it clear and answer the questions all the same, even if the answer is Rule of Cool.<br /> <br /> Making up a concept for a build isn't hard. What is hard is to finish a design without formalizing what you want out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}